  "latest_final": "The student's seemingly academic story is actually about a meal. \"Courses\" means the courses of a multi-course meal, and \"choosing courses before the deadline\" mirrors choosing from a menu/order. The student was on the HKU campus dining with a group at a restaurant/counter, facing a server, and had deliberately given the server an instruction about the student's own dishes. The student asked the server to clear away or take away the dishes before the meal was finished. Those cleared dishes were the student's own meal courses, and the other person — the server — deliberately carried out that instruction, so the student's food was removed/taken rather than kept. Thus, by the end of that evening, all of the student's courses were \"gone\": not because the university system failed, the courses were filled by competitors, or anyone sabotaged the enrollment, but because the student's own spoken request at the counter caused the server to take away the student's food courses. The \"deadline\" and \"course selection\" framing is the pun that disguised this dining mishap.",
